{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'cholinergic|nitrergic|interneuron|motor neuron|sensory neuron|Dogiel|enteric|myenteric|soma location|expresses|capable of' src/patterns/dosdp-patterns docs/patterns docs/relations_guide.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/relations_guide.md:56:### [<u>has soma location</u>](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002100)\ndocs/relations_guide.md:58:When neurobiologists talk about the location of vertebrate neurons, they are typically referring to soma location. The importance of soma location to identify is underscored by how commonly cell types are named, in part, by soma location. We therefore have a dedicated relation for recording this: [**'has soma location'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002100).\ndocs/relations_guide.md:60:For example, [anterior horn motor neuron](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_2000048) has the following subclass axiom:\ndocs/relations_guide.md:62:[**'has soma location'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002100) *some* ['ventral horn of spinal cord'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002257)\ndocs/relations_guide.md:64:**axiomatization of ‘has soma location’**\ndocs/relations_guide.md:70:-   *property chain*: has\\_soma\\_location o part\\_of --> has\\_soma\\_location \\# If x has soma location y and y is part\\_of z, then x has\\_soma\\_location\\_z\ndocs/relations_guide.md:74:'cortical interneuron' equivalentTo 'interneuron' that has\\_soma\\_location some 'cerebral cortex' \ndocs/relations_guide.md:76:'rosehip neuron' subClassOf interneuron  and has\\_soma\\_location some 'cortical layer 1' \ndocs/relations_guide.md:80:=> 'rosehip neuron' subClassOf 'cortical interneuron'\ndocs/relations_guide.md:110:To record neuron-to-neuron or motor neuron-to-target muscle connectivity, consider the following object properties. These properties should be used when connectivity is key to the definition, for example, in cases where a motor neuron type is defined by the type of muscle fiber on which it synapses.\ndocs/relations_guide.md:114:For example, ['alpha motor neuron'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0008038) SubClassOf [**synapsed to**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002120) *some* ['extrafusal muscle fiber'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0008046)\ndocs/relations_guide.md:120:For example, ['extrafusal muscle fiber'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0008046) SubClassOf [**synapsed by**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002103) *some* ['alpha motor neuron'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0008038)\ndocs/relations_guide.md:124:Cellular function is recorded by linking GO biological process terms with the object properties [**'capable of'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002215) and ‘capable of part of’\ndocs/relations_guide.md:126:###  [<u>'capable of'</u>](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002215)\ndocs/relations_guide.md:128:Use this relation where the cell is capable of carrying out the entirety of the process\ndocs/relations_guide.md:132:[**'capable of'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002215) *some* ['androgen secretion'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0035935)\ndocs/relations_guide.md:136:To record which neurotransmitter a neuron releases, use a [**'capable of'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002215) relation to link the neuron to a subclass of GO [neurotransmitter secretion](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0007269) that references a neurotransmitter type. This should be sufficient for autoclassification.\ndocs/relations_guide.md:138:e.g. ['medium spiny neuron'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_1001474) [**'capable of'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002215) some ['gamma-aminobutyric acid secretion, neurotransmission'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0061534)\ndocs/relations_guide.md:140:### ‘capable of part of’\ndocs/relations_guide.md:144:e.g.  'retinal bipolar neuron' 'capable of part of' some 'visual perception'\ndocs/relations_guide.md:188:### ‘expresses’\ndocs/relations_guide.md:194:'lamp5 GABAergic cortical interneuron' EquivalentTo:\ndocs/relations_guide.md:195:interneuron and ('has soma location' some 'cerebral cortex')\ndocs/relations_guide.md:196:and ('capable of' some 'gamma-aminobutyric acid secretion, neurotransmission') \ndocs/relations_guide.md:197:and (expresses some 'lysosome-associated membrane glycoprotein 5')\ndocs/patterns/cellBearerOfQuality.md:32:| [CL:0000103](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000103) | bipolar neuron        | [CL:0000099](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000099) | interneuron  | [PATO:0070006](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0070006) | bipolar morphology       |\ndocs/patterns/cellBearerOfQuality.md:33:| [CL:4023077](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_4023077) | bitufted neuron       | [CL:0000099](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000099) | interneuron  | [PATO:0070012](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0070012) | bitufted cell morphology |\ndocs/patterns/overview.md:23:| CL:0000103 | bipolar neuron        | CL:0000099 | interneuron  | PATO:0070006 | bipolar morphology       |\ndocs/patterns/overview.md:24:| CL:4023077 | bitufted neuron       | CL:0000099 | interneuron  | PATO:0070012 | bitufted cell morphology |\ndocs/patterns/overview.md:27:### Cell capable of biological process\ndocs/patterns/overview.md:28:*Any cell that is involved in/capable of a particular biological process, such as acid secretion.*\ndocs/patterns/overview.md:45:| CL:0011005 | GABAergic interneuron                      | GO:0061534 | gamma-aminobutyric acid secretion, neurotransmission | CL:0000099 | interneuron                     |\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/neuronHasSomaLoc:5:  gross type and soma locataion. e.g. cortical interneuron.\"\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/neuronHasSomaLoc:7:#    - http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0008031  # cortical interneuron\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/neuronHasSomaLoc:19:  has soma location: \"RO:0002100\"\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/neuronHasSomaLoc:48:  text: \"%s and ('has soma location' some %s)\"\ndocs/patterns/cellCapableOfBiologicalProcess.md:6:Any cell that is involved in/capable of a particular biological process, such as acid secretion.\ndocs/patterns/cellCapableOfBiologicalProcess.md:13:A {[cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000000)} that is capable of {[biological_process](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0008150)}.\ndocs/patterns/cellCapableOfBiologicalProcess.md:17:{[cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000000)} and ([capable of](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002215) some {[biological_process](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0008150)})\ndocs/patterns/cellCapableOfBiologicalProcess.md:25:| [CL:0011005](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0011005) | GABAergic interneuron                      | [GO:0061534](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0061534) | gamma-aminobutyric acid secretion, neurotransmission | [CL:0000099](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000099) | interneuron                     |\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/cellCapableOfBiologicalProcess.yaml:4:description: Any cell that is involved in/capable of a particular biological process, such as acid secretion.\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/cellCapableOfBiologicalProcess.yaml:12:  capable of: \"RO:0002215\"\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/cellCapableOfBiologicalProcess.yaml:25:  text: \"A %s that is capable of %s.\"\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/cellCapableOfBiologicalProcess.yaml:31:  text: \"%s and ('capable of' some %s)\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
