arvard, Cambridge, MA, USA.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Aguirre AJ\",\"firstName\":\"Andrew J\",\"lastName\":\"Aguirre\",\"initials\":\"AJ\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard, Cambridge, MA, USA; Department of Medical Oncology, Dana Farber Cancer Institute, Boston, MA, USA.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Boland GM\",\"firstName\":\"Genevieve M\",\"lastName\":\"Boland\",\"initials\":\"GM\",\"authorId\":{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0002-7522-6173\"},\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Department of Molecular Biology, Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, MA, USA.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Graham D\",\"firstName\":\"Daniel\",\"lastName\":\"Graham\",\"initials\":\"D\",\"authorId\":{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0002-8403-8115\"},\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard, Cambridge, MA, USA; Department of Molecular Biology, Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, MA, USA; Gastrointestinal Unit and Center for the Study of Inflammatory Bowel Disease, Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, MA, USA.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Rozenblatt-Rosen O\",\"firstName\":\"Orit\",\"lastName\":\"Rozenblatt-Rosen\",\"initials\":\"O\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Klarman Cell Observatory, Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard, Cambridge, MA, USA. Electronic address: orit@broadinstitute.org.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Xavier RJ\",\"firstName\":\"Ramnik J\",\"lastName\":\"Xavier\",\"initials\":\"RJ\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard, Cambridge, MA, USA; Department of Molecular Biology, Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, MA, USA; Gastrointestinal Unit and Center for the Study of Inflammatory Bowel Disease, Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, MA, USA; Center for Computational and Integrative Biology, Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, MA, USA. Electronic address: xavier@molbio.mgh.harvard.edu.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Regev A\",\"firstName\":\"Aviv\",\"lastName\":\"Regev\",\"initials\":\"A\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Klarman Cell Observatory, Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard, Cambridge, MA, USA; Howard Hughes Medical Institute and Koch Institute for Integrative Cancer Research, Department of Biology, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Cambridge, MA, USA. Electronic address: aregev@broadinstitute.org.\"}]}}]},\"authorIdList\":{\"authorId\":[{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0002-7522-6173\"},{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0002-7606-3433\"},{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0002-8403-8115\"},{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0003-2123-3906\"}]},\"dataLinksTagsList\":{\"dataLinkstag\":[\"altmetrics\",\"supporting_data\",\"related_data\"]},\"journalInfo\":{\"issue\":\"6\",\"volume\":\"182\",\"journalIssueId\":3014268,\"dateOfPublication\":\"2020 Sep\",\"monthOfPublication\":9,\"yearOfPublication\":2020,\"printPublicationDate\":\"2020-09-01\",\"journal\":{\"title\":\"Cell\",\"medlineAbbreviation\":\"Cell\",\"essn\":\"1097-4172\",\"isoabbreviation\":\"Cell\",\"issn\":\"0092-8674\",\"nlmid\":\"0413066\"}},\"pubYear\":\"2020\",\"pageInfo\":\"1606-1622.e23\",\"abstractText\":\"The enteric nervous system (ENS) coordinates diverse functions in the intestine but has eluded comprehensive molecular characterization because of the rarity and diversity of cells. Here we develop two methods to profile the ENS of adult mice and humans at single-cell resolution: RAISIN RNA-seq for profiling intact nuclei with ribosome-bound mRNA and MIRACL-seq for label-free enrichment of rare cell types by droplet-based profiling. The 1,187,535 nuclei in our mouse atlas include 5,068 neurons from the ileum and colon, revealing extraordinary neuron diversity. We highlight circadian expression changes in enteric neurons, show that disease-related genes are dysregulated with aging, and identify differences between the ileum and proximal/distal colon. In humans, we profile 436,202 nuclei, recovering 1,445 neurons, and identify conserved and species-specific transcriptional programs and putative neuro-epithelial, neuro-stromal, and neuro-immune interactions. The human ENS expresses risk genes for neuropathic, inflammatory, and extra-intestinal diseases, suggesting neuronal contributions to disease.\",\"affiliation\":\"Klarman Cell Observatory, Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard, Cambridge, MA, USA.\",\"publicationStatus\":\"ppublish\",\"language\":\"eng\",\"pubModel\":\"Print-Electronic\",\"pubTypeList\":{\"pubType\":[\"Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't\",\"research-article\",\"Journal Article\",\"Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural\"]},\"grantsList\":{\"grant\":[{\"grantId\":\"R01 DK117263\",\"agency\":\"NIDDK NIH HHS\",\"acronym\":\"DK\",\"orderIn\":0},{\"grantId\":\"P30 DK043351\",\"agency\":\"NIDDK NIH HHS\",\"acronym\":\"DK\",\"orderIn\":0},{\"agency\":\"Broad Institute\",\"orderIn\":0},{\"agency\":\"Crohn&apos;s and Colitis Foundation\",\"orderIn\":0},{\"agency\":\"Howard Hughes Medical Institute\",\"acronym\":\"HHMI\",\"orderIn\":0},{\"agency\":\"Klarman Cell Observatory, Broad Institute\",\"orderIn\":0},{\"grantId\":\"RC2 DK114784\",\"agency\":\"NIDDK NIH HHS\",\"acronym\":\"DK\",\"orderIn\":0},{\"grantId\":\"K08 CA218420\",\"agency\":\"NCI NIH HHS\",\"acronym\":\"CA\",\"orderIn\":0},{\"agency\":\"Leona M. and Harry B. Helmsley Charitable Trust\",\"orderIn\":0}]},\"meshHeadingList\":{\"meshHeading\":[{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Colon\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"CY\",\"qualifierName\":\"cytology\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Ileum\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"CY\",\"qualifierName\":\"cytology\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Neuroglia\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"CY\",\"qualifierName\":\"cytology\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Neurons\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"CY\",\"qualifierName\":\"cytology\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"Y\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Nissl Bodies\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"GE\",\"qualifierName\":\"genetics\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"Y\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"UL\",\"qualifierName\":\"ultrastructure\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Enteric Nervous System\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"CY\",\"qualifierName\":\"cytology\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"Y\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"Y\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Endoplasmic Reticulum, Rough\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"GE\",\"qualifierName\":\"genetics\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"UL\",\"qualifierName\":\"ultrastructure\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Ribosomes\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"UL\",\"qualifierName\":\"ultrastructure\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorNam