{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl -s 'https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:37355216&resultType=core&format=json' | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"{\"version\":\"6.9\",\"hitCount\":1,\"request\":{\"queryString\":\"EXT_ID:37355216\",\"resultType\":\"core\",\"cursorMark\":\"*\",\"pageSize\":25,\"sort\":\"\",\"synonym\":false},\"resultList\":{\"result\":[{\"id\":\"37355216\",\"source\":\"MED\",\"pmid\":\"37355216\",\"pmcid\":\"PMC10469081\",\"fullTextIdList\":{\"fullTextId\":[\"PMC10469081\"]},\"doi\":\"10.1016/j.jcmgh.2023.06.010\",\"title\":\"Types of Neurons in the Human Colonic Myenteric Plexus Identified by Multilayer Immunohistochemical Coding.\",\"authorString\":\"Chen BN, Humenick A, Yew WP, Peterson RA, Wiklendt L, Dinning PG, Spencer NJ, Wattchow DA, Costa M, Brookes SJH.\",\"authorList\":{\"author\":[{\"fullName\":\"Chen BN\",\"firstName\":\"Bao Nan\",\"lastName\":\"Chen\",\"initials\":\"BN\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, South Australia, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Humenick A\",\"firstName\":\"Adam\",\"lastName\":\"Humenick\",\"initials\":\"A\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, South Australia, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Yew WP\",\"firstName\":\"Wai Ping\",\"lastName\":\"Yew\",\"initials\":\"WP\",\"authorId\":{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0001-7436-0779\"},\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, South Australia, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Peterson RA\",\"firstName\":\"Rochelle A\",\"lastName\":\"Peterson\",\"initials\":\"RA\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, South Australia, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Wiklendt L\",\"firstName\":\"Lukasz\",\"lastName\":\"Wiklendt\",\"initials\":\"L\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, South Australia, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Dinning PG\",\"firstName\":\"Phil G\",\"lastName\":\"Dinning\",\"initials\":\"PG\",\"authorId\":{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0001-8910-2801\"},\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, South Australia, Australia; Colorectal Surgical Unit, Division of Surgery, Flinders Medical Centre, Bedford Park, South Australia, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Spencer NJ\",\"firstName\":\"Nick J\",\"lastName\":\"Spencer\",\"initials\":\"NJ\",\"authorId\":{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0003-2190-5303\"},\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, South Australia, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Wattchow DA\",\"firstName\":\"David A\",\"lastName\":\"Wattchow\",\"initials\":\"DA\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Colorectal Surgical Unit, Division of Surgery, Flinders Medical Centre, Bedford Park, South Australia, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Costa M\",\"firstName\":\"Marcello\",\"lastName\":\"Costa\",\"initials\":\"M\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, South Australia, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Brookes SJH\",\"firstName\":\"Simon J H\",\"lastName\":\"Brookes\",\"initials\":\"SJH\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, South Australia, Australia. Electronic address: simon.brookes@flinders.edu.au.\"}]}}]},\"authorIdList\":{\"authorId\":[{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0001-7436-0779\"},{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0001-8910-2801\"},{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0003-2190-5303\"}]},\"dataLinksTagsList\":{\"dataLinkstag\":[\"altmetrics\",\"recommended_reviews\"]},\"journalInfo\":{\"issue\":\"4\",\"volume\":\"16\",\"journalIssueId\":3636764,\"dateOfPublication\":\"2023 \",\"monthOfPublication\":0,\"yearOfPublication\":2023,\"printPublicationDate\":\"2023-01-01\",\"journal\":{\"title\":\"Cellular and molecular gastroenterology and hepatology\",\"medlineAbbreviation\":\"Cell Mol Gastroenterol Hepatol\",\"essn\":\"2352-345X\",\"issn\":\"2352-345X\",\"nlmid\":\"101648302\",\"isoabbreviation\":\"Cell Mol Gastroenterol Hepatol\"}},\"pubYear\":\"2023\",\"pageInfo\":\"573-605\",\"abstractText\":\"<h4>Background and aims</h4>Gut functions including motility, secretion, and blood flow are largely controlled by the enteric nervous system. Characterizing the different classes of enteric neurons in the human gut is an important step to understand how its circuitry is organized and how it is affected by disease.<h4>Methods</h4>Using multiplexed immunohistochemistry, 12 discriminating antisera were applied to distinguish different classes of myenteric neurons in the human colon (2596 neurons, 12 patients) according to their chemical coding. All antisera were applied to every neuron, in multiple layers, separated by elutions.<h4>Results</h4>A total of 164 combinations of immunohistochemical markers were present among the 2596 neurons, which could be divided into 20 classes, with statistical validation. Putative functions were ascribed for 4 classes of putative excitatory motor neurons (EMN1-4), 4 inhibitory motor neurons (IMN1-4), 3 ascending interneurons (AIN1-3), 6 descending interneurons (DIN1-6), 2 classes of multiaxonal sensory neurons (SN1-2), and a small, miscellaneous group (1.8% of total). Soma-dendritic morphology was analyzed, revealing 5 common shapes distributed differentially between the 20 classes. Distinctive baskets of axonal varicosities surrounded 45% of myenteric nerve cell bodies and were associated with close appositions, suggesting possible connectivity. Baskets of cholinergic terminals and several other types of baskets selectively targeted ascending interneurons and excitatory motor neurons but were significantly sparser around inhibitory motor neurons.<h4>Conclusions</h4>Using a simple immunohistochemical method, human myenteric neurons were shown to comprise multiple classes based on chemical coding and morphology and dense clusters of axonal varicosities were selectively associated with some classes.\",\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, South Australia, Australia.\",\"publicationStatus\":\"ppublish\",\"language\":\"eng\",\"pubModel\":\"Print-Electronic\",\"pubTypeList\":{\"pubType\":[\"research-article\",\"Journal Article\",\"Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural\"]},\"grantsList\":{\"grant\":[{\"grantId\":\"OT2 OD024899\",\"agency\":\"NIH HHS\",\"acronym\":\"OD\",\"orderIn\":0},{\"grantId\":\"OT2OD24899\",\"agency\":\"National Institutes of Health\",\"orderIn\":0},{\"agency\":\"University of California, Los Angeles\",\"orderIn\":0}]},\"meshHeadingList\":{\"meshHeading\":[{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Colon\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"IR\",\"qualifierName\":\"innervation\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Neurons, Afferent\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Motor Neurons\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"Y\",\"descriptorName\":\"Myenteric Plexus\"},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"Y\",\"descriptorName\":\"Enteric Nervous System\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Humans\"}]},\"keywordList\":{\"keyword\":[\"Immunofluorescence\",\"Antisera\",\"Enteric nervous system\",\"Classes\"]},\"subsetList\":{\"subset\":[{\"code\":\"IM\",\"name\":\"Index Medicus\"}]},\"fullTextUrlList\":{\"fullTextUrl\":[{\"availability\":\"Subscription required\",\"availabilityCode\":\"S\",\"documentStyle\":\"doi\",\"site\":\"DOI\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcmgh.2023.06.010\"},{\"availability\":\"Open access\",\"availabilityCode\":\"OA\",\"documentStyle\":\"html\",\"site\":\"Europe_PMC\",\"url\":\"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10469081\"},{\"availability\":\"Open access\",\"availabilityCode\":\"OA\",\"documentStyle\":\"pdf\",\"site\":\"Europe_PMC\",\"url\":\"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10469081?pdf=render\"}]},\"isOpenAccess\":\"Y\",\"inEPMC\":\"Y\",\"inPMC\":\"Y\",\"hasPDF\":\"Y\",\"hasBook\":\"N\",\"hasSuppl\":\"N\",\"citedByCount\":11,\"hasData\":\"N\",\"hasReferences\":\"Y\",\"hasTextMinedTerms\":\"Y\",\"hasDbCrossReferences\":\"N\",\"hasLabsLinks\":\"Y\",\"license\":\"cc by-nc-nd\",\"hasEvaluations\":\"N\",\"authMan\":\"N\",\"epmcAuthMan\":\"N\",\"nihAuthMan\":\"N\",\"hasTMAccessionNumbers\":\"N\",\"dateOfCompletion\":\"2023-09-22\",\"dateOfCreation\":\"2023-06-24\",\"firstIndexDate\":\"2023-06-25\",\"fullTextReceivedDate\":\"2023-09-02\",\"dateOfRevision\":\"2023-09-22\",\"electronicPublicationDate\":\"2023-06-22\",\"firstPublicationDate\":\"2023-06-22\"}]}}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl -s 'https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:34170401&resultType=core&format=json' | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"{\"version\":\"6.9\",\"hitCount\":1,\"request\":{\"queryString\":\"EXT_ID:34170401\",\"resultType\":\"core\",\"cursorMark\":\"*\",\"pageSize\":25,\"sort\":\"\",\"synonym\":false},\"resultList\":{\"result\":[{\"id\":\"34170401\",\"source\":\"MED\",\"pmid\":\"34170401\",\"pmcid\":\"PMC8397665\",\"fullTextIdList\":{\"fullTextId\":[\"PMC8397665\"]},\"doi\":\"10.1007/s00418-021-02002-y\",\"title\":\"Classification of human enteric neurons.\",\"authorString\":\"Brehmer A.\",\"authorList\":{\"author\":[{\"fullName\":\"Brehmer A\",\"firstName\":\"Axel\",\"lastName\":\"Brehmer\",\"initials\":\"A\",\"authorId\":{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0002-9667-0070\"},\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Institute of Anatomy and Cell Biology, Friedrich-Alexander Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg, Krankenhausstr. 9, 91054, Erlangen, Germany. axel.brehmer@fau.de.\"}]}}]},\"authorIdList\":{\"authorId\":[{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0002-9667-0070\"}]},\"journalInfo\":{\"issue\":\"2\",\"volume\":\"156\",\"journalIssueId\":3223494,\"dateOfPublication\":\"2021 Aug\",\"monthOfPublication\":8,\"yearOfPublication\":2021,\"printPublicationDate\":\"2021-08-01\",\"journal\":{\"title\":\"Histochemistry and cell biology\",\"medlineAbbreviation\":\"Histochem Cell Biol\",\"essn\":\"1432-119X\",\"issn\":\"0948-6143\",\"nlmid\":\"9506663\",\"isoabbreviation\":\"Histochem Cell Biol\"}},\"pubYear\":\"2021\",\"pageInfo\":\"95-108\",\"abstractText\":\"Major advances in our understanding of the functional heterogeneity of enteric neurons are driven by the application of newly developed, innovative methods. In contrast to this progress, both animal and human enteric neurons are usually divided into only two morphological subpopulations, \\\"Dogiel type II\\\" neurons (with several long processes) and \\\"Dogiel type I\\\" neurons (with several short processes). This implies no more than the distinction of intrinsic primary afferent from all other enteric neurons. The well-known chemical and functional diversity of enteric neurons is not reflected by this restrictive dichotomy of morphological data. Recent structural investigations of human enteric neurons were performed by different groups which mainly used two methodical approaches, namely detecting the architecture of their processes and target-specific tracing of their axonal courses. Both methods were combined with multiple immunohistochemistry in order to decipher neurochemical codes. This review integrates these morphological and immunohistological data and presents a classification of human enteric neurons which we believe is not yet complete but provides an essential foundation for the further development of human gastrointestinal neuropathology.\",\"affiliation\":\"Institute of Anatomy and Cell Biology, Friedrich-Alexander Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg, Krankenhausstr. 9, 91054, Erlangen, Germany. axel.brehmer@fau.de.\",\"publicationStatus\":\"ppublish\",\"language\":\"eng\",\"pubModel\":\"Print-Electronic\",\"pubTypeList\":{\"pubType\":[\"review-article\",\"Review\",\"Journal Article\"]},\"grantsList\":{\"grant\":[{\"agency\":\"Friedrich-Alexander-Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg\",\"orderIn\":0}]},\"meshHeadingList\":{\"meshHeading\":[{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Neurons\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"PA\",\"qualifierName\":\"pathology\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"Y\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Enteric Nervous System\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"PA\",\"qualifierName\":\"pathology\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"Y\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Humans\"},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Immunohistochemistry\"}]},\"keywordList\":{\"keyword\":[\"Enteric nervous system\",\"Neuroanatomical Terminology\",\"Stach\",\"Dogiel\"]},\"subsetList\":{\"subset\":[{\"code\":\"IM\",\"name\":\"Index Medicus\"}]},\"fullTextUrlList\":{\"fullTextUrl\":[{\"availability\":\"Subscription required\",\"availabilityCode\":\"S\",\"documentStyle\":\"doi\",\"site\":\"DOI\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00418-021-02002-y\"},{\"availability\":\"Open access\",\"availabilityCode\":\"OA\",\"documentStyle\":\"html\",\"site\":\"Europe_PMC\",\"url\":\"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC8397665\"},{\"availability\":\"Open access\",\"availabilityCode\":\"OA\",\"documentStyle\":\"pdf\",\"site\":\"Europe_PMC\",\"url\":\"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC8397665?pdf=render\"}]},\"isOpenAccess\":\"Y\",\"inEPMC\":\"Y\",\"inPMC\":\"Y\",\"hasPDF\":\"Y\",\"hasBook\":\"N\",\"hasSuppl\":\"N\",\"citedByCount\":40,\"hasData\":\"N\",\"hasReferences\":\"Y\",\"hasTextMinedTerms\":\"Y\",\"hasDbCrossReferences\":\"N\",\"hasLabsLinks\":\"N\",\"license\":\"cc by\",\"hasEvaluations\":\"N\",\"authMan\":\"N\",\"epmcAuthMan\":\"N\",\"nihAuthMan\":\"N\",\"hasTMAccessionNumbers\":\"N\",\"dateOfCompletion\":\"2021-10-19\",\"dateOfCreation\":\"2021-06-25\",\"firstIndexDate\":\"2021-06-26\",\"fullTextReceivedDate\":\"2025-02-04\",\"dateOfRevision\":\"2022-05-31\",\"electronicPublicationDate\":\"2021-06-25\",\"firstPublicationDate\":\"2021-06-25\"}]}}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl -s 'https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:38292899&resultType=core&format=json' | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"{\"version\":\"6.9\",\"hitCount\":1,\"request\":{\"queryString\":\"EXT_ID:38292899\",\"resultType\":\"core\",\"cursorMark\":\"*\",\"pageSize\":25,\"sort\":\"\",\"synonym\":false},\"resultList\":{\"result\":[{\"id\":\"38292899\",\"source\":\"MED\",\"pmid\":\"38292899\",\"pmcid\":\"PMC10825022\",\"fullTextIdList\":{\"fullTextId\":[\"PMC10825022\"]},\"doi\":\"10.3389/fnins.2023.1313057\",\"title\":\"Characterization of viscerofugal neurons in human colon by retrograde tracing and multi-layer immunohistochemistry.\",\"authorString\":\"Chen BN, Humenick AG, Hibberd TJ, Yew WP, Wattchow DA, Dinning PG, Costa M, Spencer NJ, Brookes SJH.\",\"authorList\":{\"author\":[{\"fullName\":\"Chen BN\",\"firstName\":\"Bao Nan\",\"lastName\":\"Chen\",\"initials\":\"BN\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, Medical Bioscience, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, SA, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Humenick AG\",\"firstName\":\"Adam G\",\"lastName\":\"Humenick\",\"initials\":\"AG\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, Medical Bioscience, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, SA, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Hibberd TJ\",\"firstName\":\"Timothy James\",\"lastName\":\"Hibberd\",\"initials\":\"TJ\",\"authorId\":{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0002-3747-140X\"},\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, Medical Bioscience, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, SA, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Yew WP\",\"firstName\":\"Wai Ping\",\"lastName\":\"Yew\",\"initials\":\"WP\",\"authorId\":{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0001-7436-0779\"},\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, Medical Bioscience, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, SA, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Wattchow DA\",\"firstName\":\"David A\",\"lastName\":\"Wattchow\",\"initials\":\"DA\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Department of Surgery, Flinders Medical Centre, Bedford Park, SA, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Dinning PG\",\"firstName\":\"Phil G\",\"lastName\":\"Dinning\",\"initials\":\"PG\",\"authorId\":{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0001-8910-2801\"},\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Department of Surgery, Flinders Medical Centre, Bedford Park, SA, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Costa M\",\"firstName\":\"Marcello\",\"lastName\":\"Costa\",\"initials\":\"M\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, Medical Bioscience, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, SA, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Spencer NJ\",\"firstName\":\"Nick J\",\"lastName\":\"Spencer\",\"initials\":\"NJ\",\"authorId\":{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0003-2190-5303\"},\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, Medical Bioscience, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, SA, Australia.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Brookes SJH\",\"firstName\":\"Simon J H\",\"lastName\":\"Brookes\",\"initials\":\"SJH\",\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, Medical Bioscience, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, SA, Australia.\"}]}}]},\"authorIdList\":{\"authorId\":[{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0001-7436-0779\"},{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0001-8910-2801\"},{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0002-3747-140X\"},{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0003-2190-5303\"}]},\"dataLinksTagsList\":{\"dataLinkstag\":[\"altmetrics\",\"supporting_data\"]},\"journalInfo\":{\"volume\":\"17\",\"journalIssueId\":3500595,\"dateOfPublication\":\"2023 \",\"monthOfPublication\":0,\"yearOfPublication\":2023,\"printPublicationDate\":\"2023-01-01\",\"journal\":{\"title\":\"Frontiers in neuroscience\",\"medlineAbbreviation\":\"Front Neurosci\",\"essn\":\"1662-453X\",\"issn\":\"1662-4548\",\"nlmid\":\"101478481\",\"isoabbreviation\":\"Front Neurosci\"}},\"pubYear\":\"2023\",\"pageInfo\":\"1313057\",\"abstractText\":\"<h4>Background and aims</h4>Viscerofugal neurons (VFNs) have cell bodies in the myenteric plexus and axons that project to sympathetic prevertebral ganglia. In animals they activate sympathetic motility reflexes and may modulate glucose metabolism and feeding. We used rapid retrograde tracing from colonic nerves to identify VFNs in human colon for the first time, using <i>ex vivo</i> preparations with multi-layer immunohistochemistry.<h4>Methods</h4>Colonic nerves were identified in isolated preparations of human colon and set up for axonal tracing with biotinamide. After fixation, labeled VFN cell bodies were subjected to multiplexed immunohistochemistry for 12 established nerve cell body markers.<h4>Results</h4>Biotinamide tracing filled 903 viscerofugal nerve cell bodies (<i>n</i> = 23), most of which (85%) had axons projecting orally before entering colonic nerves. Morphologically, 97% of VFNs were uni-axonal. Of 215 VFNs studied in detail, 89% expressed ChAT, 13% NOS, 13% calbindin, 9% enkephalin, 7% substance P and 0 of 123 VFNs expressed CART. Few VFNs contained calretinin, VIP, 5HT, CGRP, or NPY. VFNs were often surrounded by dense baskets of axonal varicosities, probably reflecting patterns of connectivity; VAChT+ (cholinergic), SP+ and ENK+ varicosities were most abundant around them. Human VFNs were diverse; showing 27 combinations of immunohistochemical markers, 4 morphological types and a wide range of cell body sizes. However, 69% showed chemical coding, axonal projections, soma-dendritic morphology and connectivity similar to enteric excitatory motor neurons.<h4>Conclusion</h4>Viscerofugal neurons are present in human colon and show very diverse combinations of features. High proportions express ChAT, consistent with cholinergic synaptic outputs onto postganglionic sympathetic neurons in prevertebral ganglia.\",\"affiliation\":\"Human Physiology, Medical Bioscience, College of Medicine and Public Health, Flinders University, Adelaide, SA, Australia.\",\"publicationStatus\":\"epublish\",\"language\":\"eng\",\"pubModel\":\"Electronic-eCollection\",\"pubTypeList\":{\"pubType\":[\"research-article\",\"Journal Article\"]},\"grantsList\":{\"grant\":[{\"grantId\":\"OT2 OD024899\",\"agency\":\"NIH HHS\",\"acronym\":\"OD\",\"orderIn\":0}]},\"keywordList\":{\"keyword\":[\"Colon\",\"Enteric nervous system\",\"Viscerofugal\",\"Multiplexed Immunohistochemistry\",\"Intestinofugal\"]},\"fullTextUrlList\":{\"fullTextUrl\":[{\"availability\":\"Open access\",\"availabilityCode\":\"OA\",\"documentStyle\":\"pdf\",\"site\":\"Unpaywall\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fnins.2023.1313057/pdf?isPublishedV2=False\"},{\"availability\":\"Subscription required\",\"availabilityCode\":\"S\",\"documentStyle\":\"doi\",\"site\":\"DOI\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2023.1313057\"},{\"availability\":\"Open access\",\"availabilityCode\":\"OA\",\"documentStyle\":\"html\",\"site\":\"Europe_PMC\",\"url\":\"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10825022\"},{\"availability\":\"Open access\",\"availabilityCode\":\"OA\",\"documentStyle\":\"pdf\",\"site\":\"Europe_PMC\",\"url\":\"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10825022?pdf=render\"}]},\"isOpenAccess\":\"Y\",\"inEPMC\":\"Y\",\"inPMC\":\"Y\",\"hasPDF\":\"Y\",\"hasBook\":\"N\",\"hasSuppl\":\"Y\",\"citedByCount\":4,\"hasData\":\"Y\",\"hasReferences\":\"Y\",\"hasTextMinedTerms\":\"Y\",\"hasDbCrossReferences\":\"N\",\"hasLabsLinks\":\"Y\",\"license\":\"cc by\",\"hasEvaluations\":\"N\",\"authMan\":\"N\",\"epmcAuthMan\":\"N\",\"nihAuthMan\":\"N\",\"hasTMAccessionNumbers\":\"N\",\"dateOfCreation\":\"2024-01-31\",\"firstIndexDate\":\"2024-01-31\",\"fullTextReceivedDate\":\"2024-02-02\",\"dateOfRevision\":\"2024-10-23\",\"electronicPublicationDate\":\"2024-01-16\",\"firstPublicationDate\":\"2024-01-16\"}]}}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
