/s00441-010-0954-z.</cite> [<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00441-010-0954-z\" class=\"usa-link usa-link--external\" data-ga-action=\"click_feat_suppl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DOI</a>] [<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20336467/\" class=\"usa-link\">PubMed</a>] [<a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?journal=Cell%20Tissue%20Res&amp;title=Immunohistochemical%20characteristics%20of%20submucosal%20Dogiel%20type%20II%20neurons%20in%20rat%20colon&amp;author=R%20Mitsui&amp;volume=340&amp;issue=2&amp;publication_year=2010&amp;pages=257-265&amp;pmid=20336467&amp;doi=10.1007/s00441-010-0954-z&amp;\" class=\"usa-link usa-link--external\" data-ga-action=\"click_feat_suppl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Google Scholar</a>]</li>\n1829:<cite>Portbury AL, Pompolo S, Furness JB, Stebbing MJ, Kunze WA, Bornstein JC, Hughes S. Cholinergic, somatostatin-immunoreactive interneurons in the guinea pig intestine: morphology, ultrastructure, connections and projections. J Anat. 1995;187(Pt 2):303–321.</cite> [<a href=\"/articles/PMC1167426/\" class=\"usa-link\">PMC free article</a>] [<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7591994/\" class=\"usa-link\">PubMed</a>] [<a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?journal=J%20Anat&amp;title=Cholinergic,%20somatostatin-immunoreactive%20interneurons%20in%20the%20guinea%20pig%20intestine:%20morphology,%20ultrastructure,%20connections%20and%20projections&amp;author=AL%20Portbury&amp;author=S%20Pompolo&amp;author=JB%20Furness&amp;author=MJ%20Stebbing&amp;author=WA%20Kunze&amp;volume=187&amp;issue=Pt%202&amp;publication_year=1995&amp;pages=303-321&amp;pmid=7591994&amp;\" class=\"usa-link usa-link--external\" data-ga-action=\"click_feat_suppl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Google Scholar</a>]</li>\n1835:<cite>Porter AJ, Wattchow DA, Brookes SJ, Costa M. Cholinergic and nitrergic interneurones in the myenteric plexus of the human colon. Gut. 2002;51(1):70–75. doi