{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'RO_0002131|RO:0002131|innerv|synapsed to|axon' docs/relations_guide.md src/ontology/cl-edit.owl | sed -n '1,120p'\"","aggregated_output":"docs/relations_guide.md:50:[**'part of'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050) applies in cases where an entire cell is within an anatomical structure, but some cells have parts in multiple anatomical structures. For example, many neurons span multiple regions of the central nervous system. The general relation for this is [**overlaps**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002131) (has some part in).\ndocs/relations_guide.md:52:[**overlaps**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002131) is not currently used directly in the cell ontology (time of writing 05/2023), but more specific relationships exist for recording the location of neurons and their parts. These are described in the next section.\ndocs/relations_guide.md:112:### [<u>synapsed to</u>](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002120)\ndocs/relations_guide.md:114:For example, ['alpha motor neuron'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0008038) SubClassOf [**synapsed to**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002120) *some* ['extrafusal muscle fiber'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0008046)\ndocs/relations_guide.md:118:-   This is the the inverse of [**synapsed to**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002120)\ndocs/relations_guide.md:271:## Taxon constraints\ndocs/relations_guide.md:274:<https://oboacademy.github.io/obook/explanation/taxon-constraints-explainer/>.\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:21:Prefix(ncbitaxon:=<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ncbitaxon#>)\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:3366:Declaration(Class(obo:NCBITaxon_10090))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:3367:Declaration(Class(obo:NCBITaxon_4896))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:3368:Declaration(Class(obo:NCBITaxon_6157))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:3369:Declaration(Class(obo:NCBITaxon_6237))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:3370:Declaration(Class(obo:NCBITaxon_6657))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:3371:Declaration(Class(obo:NCBITaxon_9606))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:3372:Declaration(Class(obo:NCBITaxon_9789))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:3373:Declaration(Class(obo:NCBITaxon_9986))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:3760:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_131567))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:3980:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000023 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_33208))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:4055:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000031 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_7742))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:4768:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D007395\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000099 \"Most generally any neuron which is not motor or sensory. Interneurons may also refer to neurons whose axons remain within a particular brain region as contrasted with projection neurons which have axons projecting to other brain regions.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:4807:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0444009442\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000103 \"A type of interneuron that has two neurites, usually an axon and a dendrite, extending from opposite poles of an ovoid cell body.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:4815:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:67287\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000104 \"A neuron with three or more neurites, usually an axon and multiple dendrites.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:4883:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34696823\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37608556\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000112 \"A neuron of the invertebrate central nervous system. This neuron innervates the central complex (CX) of an invertebrate brain and it forms columnar patterns with its dendrites. It is involved in navigation and spatial processing.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:4923:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:cvs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000116 \"Pioneer neurons establish a pathway in the developing central nervous system and then undergo programmed cell death once the adult axons, which follow them, have made connections with the target site. Thus, they are a transient cell type involved in axon guidance.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:4935:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Basket_cell&oldid=951703880\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000118 \"Basket cells are inhibitory GABAergic interneurons of the brain. In general, dendrites of basket cells are free branching and contain smooth spines. Axons are highly branched. The branched axonal arborizations give rise to basket-like structures that surround the soma of the target cell. Basket cells form axo-somatic synapses, meaning their synapses target somas of other cells.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:4943:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"NIFSTD:sao1415726815\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000119 \"Large intrinsic neuron located in the granule layer of the cerebellar cortex that extends its dendrites into the molecular layer where they receive contact from parallel fibers. The axon of the Golgi cell ramifies densely in the granule layer and enters into a complex arrangement with mossy fiber terminals and granule cell dendrites to form the cerebellar glomerulus. Llinas, Walton and Lang. In The Synaptic Organization of the Brain. 5th ed. 2004.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:4959:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/granule+cell>) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000120 \"A neuron of the vertebrate central nervous system that is small in size. This general class includes small neurons in the granular layer of the cerebellar cortex, cerebral cortex neurons that are not pyramidal cells and small neurons without axons found in the olfactory bulb.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:4996:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000123 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_7742))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:5042:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009836\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oligodendrocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000128 \"A class of large neuroglial (macroglial) cells in the central nervous system. Form the insulating myelin sheath of axons in the central nervous system.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:5078:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000130 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_33317))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:5667:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0323052908\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000190 \"A muscle cell that can develop high tension rapidly. It is usually innervated by a single alpha neuron.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:5888:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:cvs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D012583\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000218 \"A neuroglial cell of the peripheral nervous system which forms the insulating myelin sheaths of peripheral axons.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:6153:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"VHOG:0001484\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000247 \"Type of neuron that is a primary mechanosensory cell, with peripheral neurites innervating the skin with free nerve endings.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:6214:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000255 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_2759)))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:6225:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000257 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_142796)))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:6801:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000338 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_33317))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:6811:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000339 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_7742))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:6822:AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0000341 obo:NCBITaxon_33511)\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:6831:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000342 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_7742))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7006:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000365 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0010017 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_33208)))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7050:AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0000371 obo:NCBITaxon_33208)\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7067:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000373 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_50557))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7144:AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0000385 obo:NCBITaxon_33511)\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7160:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000387 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_6656))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7179:AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0000390 obo:NCBITaxon_33511)\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7329:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000411 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_6237))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7377:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000418 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_6237))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7454:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000429 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_50557))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7549:SubClassOf(Annotation(obo:IAO_0000233 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1943\") obo:CL_0000441 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_6656))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7726:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000462 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_50557))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7734:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000463 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_6656))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7750:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000465 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_6656))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7776:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000468 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_33317))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7846:SubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:source <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/589>) obo:CL_0000477 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_50557))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:7923:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000487 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_6656))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:8172:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000518 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_7742))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:8177:AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0000519 obo:NCBITaxon_33511)\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:8183:AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0000520 obo:NCBITaxon_2759)\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:8191:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000521 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_4751)))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:8261:SubClassOf(Annotation(obo:IAO_0000233 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/pull/1950\") obo:CL_0000530 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_32443))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:8271:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17971221\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35431796\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000532 \"A primary motor neuron with its soma in the caudal region of a spinal cord. The axon of this motoneuron exit the spinal cord from one single point and innervates the lateral surface of ventral axial muscles\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:8298:SubClassOf(Annotation(obo:IAO_0000233 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/pull/1950\") obo:CL_0000535 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_32443))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:8329:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009474\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neuron\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000540 \"The basic cellular unit of nervous tissue. Each neuron consists of a body, an axon, and dendrites. Their purpose is to receive, conduct, and transmit impulses in the nervous system.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:8362:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000542 \"Editors note: consider adding taxon constraint to vertebrata (PMID:18025161)\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:8596:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D025042\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Amacrine_cell&oldid=1023572246\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000561 \"Interneuron of the vertebrate retina. They integrate, modulate, and interpose a temporal domain in the visual message presented to the retinal ganglion cells, with which they synapse in the inner plexiform layer. They lack large axons.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:8606:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000561 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_7742))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:8951:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D017966\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000598 \"Pyramidal neurons have a pyramid-shaped soma with a single axon, a large apical dendrite and multiple basal dendrites. The apex and an apical dendrite typically point toward the pial surface and other dendrites and an axon emerging from the base. The axons may have local collaterals but also project outside their region. Pyramidal neurons are found in the cerebral cortex, the hippocampus, and the amygdala.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:9200:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:mah\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41598-018-27692-8\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000626 \"A granule cell that has a soma located in an olfactory bulb granule cell layer. An olfactory granule cell is an interneuron that lacks an axon, makes reciprocal dendro-dendritic synapses with mitral cells and tufted cells and is involved in the fine spatio-temporal tuning of the responses of these principal olfactory bulb neurons to odors.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:9385:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0412046911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31915267\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pituicyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000645 \"A glial cell of astrocytic lineage with long processes running parallel to adjacent axons in the proximal infundibulum of the neurohypophysis. These processes form a three-dimensional network among the axons of the hypothalamic neurosecretory cells and are connected by gap junctions which provide for their metabolic coupling. This cell type constitutes most of the nonexcitable tissue in the neurohypophsis; function may include possibly acting as an intermediate in the modulation of oxytocin and vasopressin release. This cell type is highly variable in size and shape and commonly contain lipid droplets and deposits of lipochrome pigment.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:9466:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16687276\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinealocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000652 \"This cell type produces and secretes melatonin and forms the pineal parenchyma. Extending from each cell body, which has a spherical, oval or lobulated mucleus, are one or more tortuous basophilic processes, containing parallel microtubules known as synaptic ribbons. These processes end in expanded terminal buds near capillaries or less, frequently, ependymal cells of the pineal recess. The terminal buds contain granular endoplasmic reticulum, mitochondria and electron-dense cored vesicles, which store monoamines and polypeptide hormones, release of which appears to require sympathetic innervation.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:9687:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17560562\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31693445\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000678 \"A neuron with soma location in the central nervous system that project its axon to the contralateral side of a central nervous system. This neuron can have its soma in the spinal cord, in the hemisphere of the brain, in the retina or in the ventral nerve cord of invertebrates.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:9688:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25960414\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27532244\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31514748\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33438755\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000678 \"Historically, commissural neurons, particularly in the spinal cord, have been used as a model to understand axon guidance during development.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:9808:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17122314\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000693 \"An interneuron that has spider-like appearance with a small round soma, a large number (7-10) of short, smooth, or slightly beaded primary dendrites that give rise to only a few secondary branches, and a branched axon that establishes a dense axonal mesh with thin shafts.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:9825:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10600995\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34047341\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36774666\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37775311\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9728912\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000695 \"A type of transient, early-born glutamatergic neuron located primarily in the marginal zone (future layer I) of the developing cerebral cortex and hippocampus in vertebrates. it is characterized by a bipolar morphology with an elongated soma, a single thick dendrite oriented toward the pial surface, and a long, thin axon that extends tangentially to form horizontal plexuses across the cortical surface. It is important for the multiple developmental processes including migration, dendritogenesis and synaptogenesis. It typically undergoes programmed cell death following cortical maturation with species- and region specific patterns of survival. In mice, it is predominantly observed in the hippocampal formation, particularly in the stratum lacunosum-moleculare and outer molecular layer of the dentate gyrus (van Bruggen et al., 2023). In contrast, in humans, a second morphologically distinct subpopulation emerges mid-gestation and persists postnatally, with surviving cells observed in the cortical sulci and the hippocampus.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10002:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15582775\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000717 \"OBSOLETE. A subset of motor neurons that innervates intrafusal muscle fibers and has small diameter axons.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10038:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000722 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_6656))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10071:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000727 \"Obsoleted as this level of precision is deemed unnecessary for CL. Consider using either the more general CL:0001658 or, if you need to refer to primary pigment cells specifically, a term from a taxon-specific ontology such as FBbt:00004231.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10078:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000728 \"Obsoleted as this level of precision is deemed unnecessary for CL. Consider using either the more general CL:0001658 or, if you need to refer to secondary pigment cells specifically, a term from a taxon-specific ontology such as FBbt:00004232.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10085:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000729 \"Obsoleted as this level of precision is deemed unnecessary for CL. Consider using either the more general CL:0001658 or, if you need to refer to tertiary pigment cells specifically, a term from a taxon-specific ontology such as FBbt:00004233.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10162:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000738 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_7742))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10173:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dph\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000740 \"The set of neurons that receives neural inputs via bipolar, horizontal and amacrine cells. The axons of these cells make up the optic nerve.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10187:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16267219\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000741 \"A motor neuron that is located in the cervical region of the spinal cord and selectively innervates the sternocleidmastoid or trapezius muscle. Unlike other motor neurons, they extend axons dorsally along lateral margins of the spinal cord.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10278:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38627529\") obo:RO_0002175 obo:CL_0000751 obo:NCBITaxon_32443)\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10296:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000753 \"An OFF-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the outer half of the inner plexiform layer. The cell body of these cells is in the middle of the inner plexiform layer. The dendritic tree is stout and the axon terminates in sublamina 1. The axonal terminal is wide and has only a few varicosities.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10305:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27565351\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000754 \"An OFF-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the outer half of the inner plexiform layer. The dendritic tree is not well filled and the dendrites are more delicate than in type 1 cells. The axon terminal is bushier and exhibits a dense plexus of varicosities in the inner part of sublamina 1 (Ghosh et al., 2004).  It can be differentiated from other retinal bipolar neurons by its expression of marker genes: Neto1, Lhx3 and Irx-6 (Shekhar, 2016).\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10315:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000755 \"An OFF-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the outer half of the inner plexiform layer. The dendritic tree is delicate and the dendritic tips appear small when compared with type 1 cells. The axon terminal is stratified and restricted to sublamina 2 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10325:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000756 \"An OFF-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the outer half of the inner plexiform layer. The cell has a diffuse axon terminal with varicosities in sublaminae 1 and 2 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10336:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000757 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. The axon terminal is restricted to sublamina 3 of the inner plexiform layer. It is narrowly stratified and branched. The dendritic tree has many delicate branches.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10345:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000758 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. The cell has a loose, delicate axon terminal that opens in sublamina 3 of the inner plexiform layer and descends into sublamina 4.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10354:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000759 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. The axon terminal is narrowly stratified and are found just below a calretinin-expressing band in sublamina 4 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10363:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000760 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. This cell has the widest dendritic field and the widest axon terminal of all retinal bipolar cells. The axon terminal is delicate and stratified through sublaminae 4 and 5 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:10373:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000761 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. The dendritic tree is wide and the dendritic convergence indicates cone selectivity. The axon terminal is sparsely branched and terminates in sublamina 5 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:12438:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000938 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000824 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_000001483) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_000002015) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001319) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0032609) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0015015 obo:PR_000001024)))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:12453:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000939 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000824 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_000002015) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001483) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0001816) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0042267) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0015016 obo:PR_000001024)))\nsrc/ontology/cl-edit.owl:12670:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000961 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000843 ObjectSome